    "/api/tts/jobs/{job_id}/release": {
      "post": {
        "description": "Surrender a claim at graceful shutdown; the consumed attempt is REFUNDED.\n\nCalled by a worker's SIGTERM handler (k8s RollingUpdate, Mac reboot). Without\nit every rollout burns one of a HEALTHY chunk's ``max_attempts`` lives and\nfour interrupted claims poison it permanently.\n\nAlways 200, never an error status: this is a shutdown path, and a worker that\nis already dying must not see something it might retry. A release that no\nlonger owns the claim (completed / reclaimed / already released) is a truthful\n``{\"released\": false}``, not a fault. If the call never lands at all, the\nserver self-heals via lease expiry.",
        "operationId": "tts.release",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "in": "path",
            "name": "job_id",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "title": "Job Id",
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/TenantIdHeader"
          }
        ],
        "requestBody": {
          "content": {
            "application/x-www-form-urlencoded": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/release"
              }
            }
          },
          "required": true
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "additionalProperties": {
                    "type": "boolean"
                  },
                  "title": "Response Tts.Release",
                  "type": "object"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Successful Response"
          },
          "422": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Validation Error"
          }
        },
        "security": [
          {
            "BearerAuth": []
          }
        ],
        "summary": "Release Claim",
        "tags": [
          "workers"
        ]
      }
    },
    "/api/tts/jobs/{job_id}/result": {
      "post": {
        "description": "Store the clip and finish the job.\n\n**Size.** Two gates protect this endpoint. ``BodySizeLimitMiddleware`` refuses an\noversized REQUEST at the ASGI layer — ahead of the multipart parser, so the body\nis never spooled to a temp file and resource exhaustion is genuinely prevented,\nnot merely converted into node disk pressure. The ``read(max + 1)`` below is the\nper-FILE bound behind it, keeping an oversized clip out of the object store.\n\n**Duration bound.** ``duration_seconds`` is persisted as ``Numeric(9, 3)``, whose\nlargest representable value is ``999999.999``. Before this bound existed, a worker\nreporting anything above it -- or ``inf``/``nan``, which ``float()`` accepts from a\nform field -- reached the UPDATE in ``job_manager`` and raised a DB ``DataError``.\nThat surfaced as a 500, the worker's ``raise_for_status()`` fired, the worker POSTed\n``/fail``, and a perfectly good job burned a retry attempt until it died. ``le`` is\nanchored on the exact column ceiling rather than ``lt=1e6`` because Postgres rounds\nto scale BEFORE checking precision, so ``999999.9995`` would round to ``1000000.000``\nand overflow; ``allow_inf_nan=False`` kills the non-finite cases outright instead of\nrelying on NaN comparison semantics, which never reject.\n\nThe bound is deliberately ONE-SIDED: there is no lower bound. A non-positive duration\nis logged below but still accepted -- see that block for why.\n\n``worker_id`` is OPTIONAL only for rollout compatibility with the manually-deployed\nMac kokoro workers (see job_manager). When present, the completion is guarded on\n``claimed_by`` so a worker whose lease already expired cannot finish the claim a\ndifferent worker now holds.\n\n**A missing measurement is not a duration of zero.** ``duration_seconds`` is\nSELF-REPORTED and is republished by ``GET /api/tts/batches/{batch_id}``, from\nwhich the orchestrator builds its narration timeline. ``tts_backend`` emits\n``duration_sec = frames / sr if sr else 0.0``, so real, good audio legitimately\narrives with NO length — a normal production event, not an attack.\n\nIt used to arrive as the number ``0.0`` and be stored as such, which made the\ngap unexpressible: the timeline builder allocated zero seconds to a chunk full\nof speech, every later chunk drifted against the picture, and the batch and the\nrun both reported success. Nothing downstream could tell that fabricated zero\nfrom a measured one.\n\nSo the field is OPTIONAL, and missing / null / non-positive are all normalised\nto ``None`` → persisted as SQL NULL (``tts_jobs.duration_seconds`` is already\nnullable) → surfaced to the consumer as ``duration_unmeasured: true`` on a job\nthat is otherwise plainly ``done``. NULL is a value the timeline builder cannot\nsilently add up, and the flag says which of the two zeroes this is.\n\nThe job is still COMPLETED — the audio is real and losing it is worse than the\ndrift. Rejecting (e.g. a ``gt=0`` bound → 422) is the trap: ``worker.py`` calls\n``raise_for_status()``, converts the 422 into a POST ``/fail``, and the queue\nrequeues a deterministically-failing job until ``max_attempts`` burns out and it\nlands in ``status='failed'`` — and the orchestrator's audiobook narrate stage\nraises ``StagePreconditionError`` on ANY failed job, aborting the whole book for\none chunk that synthesized fine.\n\nThe upper bound stays one-sided and unchanged: it exists only to keep an\nunstorable value out of ``Numeric(9, 3)``.\n\nValidating the value for real would mean decoding the clip, which is\ndeliberately out of scope here.",
        "operationId": "tts.result",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "in": "path",
            "name": "job_id",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "title": "Job Id",
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/TenantIdHeader"
          }
        ],
        "requestBody": {
          "content": {
            "multipart/form-data": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/result"
              }
            }
          },
          "required": true
        },
        "responses": {
          "204": {
            "description": "Successful Response"
          },
          "422": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Validation Error"
          }
        },
        "security": [
          {
            "BearerAuth": []
          }
        ],
        "summary": "Report Result",
        "tags": [
          "workers"
        ]
      }
    },
